# A function that takes a static list is emitted for a reference to it, even
# when no list of that type is read at run time: its parameter names the
# list's value type, so that type's C is written (the emitter's
# staticListReached, its parameter leg). Without it the C declared the
# function with a type it never defined.
show: function {xs: (staticlist text)} is {
    print "\{xs.length}"
}

main: function is {
    f: show.copy
    print "made"
}
